      "title": "RentFlow (YC S24) Is Hiring",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/rentflow/jobs/V2yneIE-senior-ai-ml-lead\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48269041\nPoints: 0\n# Comments: 0",
      "body": "Senior AI/ML Lead$130K - $200K•0.50% - 2.50%•San Francisco, CA, US / New York, NY, US / Remote (US)RoleEngineering, Machine learningConnect directly with founders of the best YC-funded startups.Apply to role ›About RentFlow\nRentFlow is tackling a hair-on-fire problem for small and medium businesses across the U.S.: the way their rent is paid each month is fundamentally misaligned with how cash actually comes in.\nWe’re building the infrastructure layer to fix that.\nToday, ~50% of U.S. businesses are late on rent in any given month. The rest face invisible struggles to pay on time, undermining their stability month after month.\nThe core issue is structural: rent hits as a single fixed lump sum on the 1st, stacked on top of every other major monthly bill, while revenue and other expenses flow in unevenly. This forces healthy businesses into recurring cash-flow stress and is a major driver of business closures.\nRentFlow is the first startup to turn fixed business rent into a cash-flow-synced product, underwritten in real time from transaction-level data to prevent issues before they even surface.\nThis opens up a $20B+ rent-splitting market and creates a natural wedge into an AI CFO layer for businesses and data opportunities we're uniquely positioned to own.\nWe're seed-stage, live since May 2025, and growing ~3x MoM. We're ramping up partnerships with the leading rent payment platforms in the U.S., fast-growing SMB software companies, and major property players.\nWe’re hiring our AI/ML lead to own underwriting, cash-flow intelligence, and data insights end-to-end.\nThis is a foundational role. You’ll design and ship models that make real financial decisions in production, affecting how and when business owners pay rent each month. You’ll work directly with the founders and have meaningful ownership over both technical direction and business outcomes.\nModel messy, real-world SMB cash flows from transaction-level data\nBuild and iterate on underwriting & decisioning systems\nLeverage LLMs to surface unique insights into business owner behavior and the forces shaping cash flow beneath the surface\nTurn raw financial data into clear, natural insights for business owners and their partners\nDesign signals that balance risk, growth, and user trust in real time\nCollaborate closely with founders on product, risk, and roadmap decisions\nShape the long-term architecture of RentFlow’s AI & data stack\nYou’ll Be a Great Fit If You\nHave built and shipped ML or data-driven systems in production\nHave worked with LLMs in production and know where to apply them\nAre comfortable working with imperfect, noisy financial data\nEnjoy high ownership, fast iteration, and ambiguous problem spaces\nWant to help define the technical DNA of an early-stage company\nAre excited to be an early hire with outsized impact, real equity, and real leverage on product and company direction\nWhy This Role Is Different\nYour models directly control real money and real outcomes\nYou’ll help define an entirely new category at the intersection of rent, finance, and AI\nYou’ll work side-by-side with founders\nYou’ll have meaningful equity and real leverage from day one\nIf you want to build something with real stakes, real users, and real impact as an early hire, we’d love to talk!\nWe’re the first startup solving a hair-on-fire problem concerning 50%+ of small & medium businesses in the US, right at a moment when the data and infrastructure make it solvable at scale.\nAt the core of what we’re solving: business rent is fixed, business cash flow isn’t. That gap forces healthy businesses into monthly cash-flow stress and is a major driver of unnecessary business closures.\nRentFlow turns fixed business rent into a cash-flow-synced product, underwriting it in real time from transaction-level data. This opens a $20B+ rent-splitting market and lets us expand into an 'AI CFO' cash-flow intelligence product for business owners and the platforms around them.\nThe product is live, growing ~3x MoM, and ramping up early partnerships with fast-growing SMB fintechs and property platforms.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
